=base:summary.cmark

How the pages of the documentation layout are sorted.

=base:main-content.cmark

The list of pages and the previous and next links of a [documentation
page](/documentation-layout.html) follow the order of the pages that use the
`documentation` layout, and only those.

# The order field

The optional `order` number of the `base:build-info.json` section gives the
position of a page: pages with a smaller number come first.

# Pages without an order

Pages without an `order` come after the numbered ones, sorted by title. A
documentation where no page has an `order` is thus sorted by title.

# Groups

The optional `group` of the `base:build-info.json` section is the name of the
group a page is listed under. The pages of a group are always listed together:
a group stands where its first page does, and its other pages follow in order.
Pages without a `group` form a group of their own, listed without a name.

# Publication status

The order only decides where a page stands among the others. A page follows the
publication status rules of any other layout.
